From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:22:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: mt7915 mac80211 ops and device init (main.c,
 init.c)

94 KUnit tests in 2 suites. In-scope coverage:
- mt7915/main.c: 0% -> 97.5% (51/51 functions)
- mt7915/init.c: 0% -> 92.0% (35/35 functions)

mt7915_init_test_device() sets up a GL-MT6000-like MT7986: an MT7976
DBDC A-die, band 0 on 2.4 GHz and band 1 on 5 GHz, 4 chains each. It
follows mt7915_register_device() minus DMA and firmware, so both wiphys
are registered with mac80211 for real.

- mt7915-main: the ieee80211_ops.
  - start and stop, interfaces and stations;
  - keys, ampdu actions and BSS changes;
  - channel config, antennas and tx power;
  - TWT, background radar and statistics.
  Each test checks the firmware commands and their fields, register values
  and driver state, with an error path for each step.
- mt7915-init:
  - band config, the ext phy, wiphy and HE/VHT/HT caps;
  - thermal and LEDs;
  - register_device with firmware that doesn't answer;
  - the full unregister_device on real DMA rings;
  - wfsys reset.

Four tests are skipped. Each one shows a suspected driver bug:
- A station's tx power set to automatic always gives -EINVAL on
  multi-chain radios (also seen from mcu.c).
- When init_hardware fails after DMA init (no firmware, say),
  register_device leaves WFDMA enabled and the rings, NAPI, dummy netdevs
  and page pools in place.
- mt7915_init_led_mux() switches on 0x7916, but the MT7916's chip id is
  0x7906, so its LED pins are never muxed.
- After set_antenna drops to one chain, the AP still advertises HE STBC
  above 80 MHz.

All tests together: 95.2% of the lines and 99.1% of the functions the
MT7986 runs (9981/10485 lines, 550/555 functions), up from 2.6%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
